# Copy to server/.env for local settings. Every setting is in src/yjsp_server/config.py.

# Local development: sign in as any email without Georgia Tech or Google, as if GT vouched for it, so a new account
# follows the whitelist (never in production).
YJSP_DEV_AUTH=1
# These emails become admins when they sign in.
YJSP_BOOTSTRAP_ADMINS=you@example.com
# To try Georgia Tech sign-in locally, set the two YJSP_MICROSOFT_ settings below: the Entra app has the redirect
# URI http://localhost:8000/auth/microsoft/callback too.

# Production (see docs/design.md, "Deploying"):
# YJSP_ENV=production
# YJSP_PUBLIC_URL=https://yjsp.example.org
# YJSP_SECRET_KEY=<python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))">
# Georgia Tech sign-in: the Entra app's Application (client) ID, and its client secret's value.
# YJSP_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# YJSP_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# YJSP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...apps.googleusercontent.com
# YJSP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# YJSP_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:////data/yjsp.db
# Vault's files (every version of every file, in blobs/). Back it up with the database:
# YJSP_VAULT_DIR=/data/vault
# Yorg's files (uploaded test data, the arrays read from it, saved scripts and models). Back it up too:
# YJSP_YORG_DIR=/data/yorg
# Where the off-site backup (deploy/yjsp-offsite, docs/deploying.md "Backups") writes how it went, for Admin > People:
# YJSP_BACKUP_STATUS=/srv/yjsp/backups/offsite.json
# Where Vault-Setup.exe (CI's vault-setup artifact) is, for the web app's SolidWorks page:
# YJSP_DOWNLOADS_DIR=/data/downloads
# Where the help's docs are (README.md, docs/, and the add-in's README, laid out as in the repository): /help shows them,
# and Claude reads them. The default is this repository; the live server keeps a copy beside the server:
# YJSP_HELP_DIR=/opt/yjsp/app/help

# Claude, in Help in the web app (docs/deploying.md, "Claude"): an Anthropic API key, a secret like the ones above; what
# it may spend each calendar month, from 00:00 UTC on the 1st (the API credits a Claude Max plan includes each month);
# what it may spend in all (credits it has once); and what one person's questions may cost in any 24 hours, in US
# dollars. Without a key and a budget (monthly, in all, or both: unset is none), Help has no Claude. Try it locally with
# a key of your own, and a budget of a few dollars.
# YJSP_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# YJSP_ASSISTANT_MONTHLY_BUDGET=95
# YJSP_ASSISTANT_BUDGET=25
# YJSP_ASSISTANT_DAILY_LIMIT=1
# Which model answers, and how hard it thinks: claude-sonnet-5-5 (the default), claude-haiku-5-5 (about a twentieth of
# the price, and weaker at working out what went wrong), or claude-opus-5-5; low, medium, high (the default), xhigh, or
# max (each slower and dearer than the last).
# YJSP_ASSISTANT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# YJSP_ASSISTANT_EFFORT=high
# Keep the help ready between questions: read it again whenever nothing has for 50 minutes, so a question hours after
# the last doesn't pay to have it read in full and kept. About $6 a month with Claude Sonnet 5.5 and the help as it is,
# counted against the budgets.
# YJSP_ASSISTANT_KEEP_WARM=1
# Another address for Anthropic's API, as a gateway's (the tests point it at a stand-in). Unset: Anthropic's own.
# YJSP_ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://gateway.example.org
